## Purpose

Kitchen Sink handbook shells (`handbook_page`, `showcase_page`), marketing layouts, and consumer sites built from `components/layouts.py` are expected to **degrade gracefully**: a reader with JavaScript disabled, a crawler, or a slow bundle should still see the **page intent**—primary headline, explanatory prose, and in-main links—without waiting for `js/` modules (`forge-theme.js`, `portal-nav.js`, `ks-diagram-catalog.js`, chart mounts, and related **Ksj** behaviors).

This deterministic rule compares two DOM snapshots of the same URL:

1. **Enabled** — metrics from the normal crawl (`wordCount`, `h1Count`, in-main links).
2. **Disabled** — Playwright reloads the page in a context with `javaScriptEnabled: false` and measures visible text inside `main#main` (or the first `main`), visible `h1` count, and `<noscript>` word count.

The check module `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-js-progressive.check.js` only evaluates pages whose enabled main copy is **substantial** (`MIN_ENABLED_MAIN_WORDS` = **96** words). It flags collapse when effective no-JS words fall below **48** and retention drops below **38%** of the enabled count (noscript text counts toward retention). Separate findings cover **missing `h1` when script is off** and **thin `<noscript>` fallbacks** when main copy still depends on script.

**Plan:** Audit content-heavy routes (handbook chapters, showcase guides, product overviews). **Do:** Emit H1, section headings, and body copy from Python generators or static HTML; gate diagrams, theme chrome, tabs, and chart data behind script. **Check:** `metrics.jsProgressiveReport` shows adequate `disabled.mainWordCount` and `disabled.h1Count`. **Adjust:** Pair with **`AI.JS.BEHAVIOR_DISCOVERABILITY`** for affordances on enhanced controls; use **`DET.JS.NO_CONSOLE_ERROR`** for console hygiene on scripted golden paths—neither replaces this noscript baseline.

## Passing signals

- **`main#main.doc-main`** (handbook column from `layouts.py`) ships a visible **`h1.font-display`**, **`p.forge-support`**, and section blocks (`forge-section`, `forge-card`, `doc-content`) in the initial HTML response—not injected only after `DOMContentLoaded`.
- **No-JS word retention** is at least **38%** of enabled main words when enabled main is at least **96** words; effective disabled words = `max(mainWordCount, noscriptWordCount)`.
- **Disabled snapshot** includes at least one visible **`h1`** inside `main` when the enabled page has an **`h1`**.
- **`<noscript>`** carries a concise intent summary (at least **12** words) when interactive surfaces (charts, diagram modals, theme picker) require script—see `generator/ux_audit_rule_pages.py` (showcase embeds do not execute inline scripts).
- **Progressive enhancements**—`data-bs-toggle`, `forge-diagram-trigger`, `data-ks-chart`, offcanvas nav—layer on top of readable static copy; disabling script leaves navigation labels and chapter prose intact.
- **`findingsFromJsProgressiveReport`** returns an empty list for harness pass fixtures and production handbook pages that server-render content.
- Thin landing stubs (enabled main under **96** words) are **skipped** intentionally—do not rely on this rule alone for sparse pages.

## Failing signals

- **`critical-text-collapse`** (**major** / **critical**): enabled main at least **96** words but no-JS effective words under **48** and retention under **0.38** — evidence like `enabled_main_words=320 nojs_main_words=8 retention=0.03`.
- **`missing-primary-heading`**: enabled `h1Count` at least **1**, disabled `h1Count` === **0** — headline injected only via script (common SPA / client-render anti-pattern).
- **`noscript-fallback`**: main still thin without script, `<noscript>` under **12** words, and no stronger collapse finding—readers get no alternate summary.
- Inline **`<script>`** that replaces `main.innerHTML` or clears the column before paint (harness defect pattern in `generator/bootstrap_missing_rule_pages.py`).
- **Empty shell**: `main` contains only a mount node (`<div id="app">`) with all copy rendered client-side.
- **Chart/diagram-only story**: prose and `h1` live inside script-built DOM; static HTML is a loading placeholder under word thresholds.
- Report **`disabled: null`** with `skippedReason` (timeout, navigation failure)—treat as audit infra issue, not a pass; re-run metrics phase.

## Before example

Failing KS markup: handbook-style `main` with only a brief `<noscript>` line while an inline script replaces the entire column with filler after load—matches the ruleset harness defect fixture.

```html
<main id="main" class="col-lg-9 col-xl-10 px-3 px-md-5 pt-4 pb-5 doc-main">
  <noscript>
    <p class="forge-support mb-3">Enable JavaScript to view this handbook chapter.</p>
  </noscript>
  <div id="ks-chapter-root" class="doc-content w-100" aria-busy="true">
    <p class="forge-support text-muted mb-0">Loading chapter…</p>
  </div>
  <script>
    (function () {
      const root = document.getElementById('ks-chapter-root');
      const main = document.getElementById('main');
      const body = Array(220).fill(
        'Governed delivery ties human intent to agent execution with review gates and evidence.'
      ).join(' ');
      const html =
        '<h1 class="font-display mb-3">Progressive enhancement</h1>' +
        '<p class="forge-support mb-4">' + body + '</p>' +
        '<section class="forge-section py-3"><div class="forge-card breathe-static p-3">' +
        '<span class="card-label">Outcome</span><p class="forge-support mb-0">Rendered only after script runs.</p>' +
        '</div></section>';
      if (root) root.innerHTML = html;
      else if (main) main.innerHTML = html;
    })();
  </script>
</main>
```

